BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:[Applied Physics/Physics Colloquium] Applied Physics/Physics Collo
 quium: Robert Huang - "High-rate qLDPC processors"
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261006T153000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261006T163000
DTSTAMP:20261006T184750Z
UID:stanford_campus-localist-54036343928909-54036343929934@local-events
DESCRIPTION:Abstract: Despite significant progress on quantum low-density 
 parity-check (qLDPC) codes\, building qLDPC processors that are high-rate
 \, high-throughput\, hardware-friendly\, and fast-to-decode remains a chal
 lenge. We introduce mitten codes\, a family of qLDPC processor codes of en
 coding rate 20% and check weight 9\, based on non-abelian groups. Their no
 n-abelian structure evades distance bounds constraining abelian counterpar
 ts\, allowing mitten codes to reach distance 18 and beyond with just a few
  h\n\nAges: All ages\nLast synced: 2026-10-06 11:47 PDT
LOCATION:Hewlett Teaching Center
END:VEVENT
